<decision #track.replace_operations_with_actions.scope apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = false confidence = 0.99 reversibility = "moderate" } (
  <question ?01M02EGVBC62AMHYDGWYX1K19X>
  How is terminology migrated?
  </?01M02EGVBC62AMHYDGWYX1K19X>
  <recommendation ?01M02EGVBC62AMHYDGWYX1K19Y>
  Use action across the release surface and retain legacy terms only in migration boundaries.
  </?01M02EGVBC62AMHYDGWYX1K19Y>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01M02EGVBC62AMHYDGWYX1K19Z>
    operations → actions 应当连文件、字符串、配置和运行时术语一起彻底改；增加 std/commands。
    </?01M02EGVBC62AMHYDGWYX1K19Z>
    <decision-text ?01M02EGVBC62AMHYDGWYX1K1A0>
    Use action everywhere in the product surface; operation remains only in explicit compatibility, migration, fixture, and historical boundaries.
    </?01M02EGVBC62AMHYDGWYX1K1A0>
    <rationale ?01M02EGVBC62AMHYDGWYX1K1A1>
    The current interface has one vocabulary while upgrade-workspace owns the supported migration path.
    </?01M02EGVBC62AMHYDGWYX1K1A1>
    <evidence ?01M02EGVBC62AMHYDGWYX1K1A2>
    Accepted Mission decision `mission.evolve_codument_action_system.action_taxonomy`.
    </?01M02EGVBC62AMHYDGWYX1K1A2>
  )>
)>
